module

public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.ExtensionByZeroCech
public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.FiniteExtensionByZeroPresentation
public import StacksCore.Tactic.StacksAttribute

/-!
# Refining a finite presentation by extensions by zero along coverings of its generators

Let `C` be a site with a distinguished collection `B` of objects satisfying the three
conditions of Stacks 0937, let `R` be a sheaf of rings on `C`, and let

`f : ⊕_{j = 1, …, m} j_{V_j!} O_{V_j} ⟶ ⊕_{i = 1, …, n} j_{U_i!} O_{U_i}`

be a morphism between finite direct sums of extensions by zero of the structure sheaf at
distinguished objects. Given coverings `{U_ik → U_i}_{k ∈ K_i}` by distinguished objects,
**Stacks 093F** says that finite subfamilies `K'_i ⊆ K_i` and a finite family `{W_l}` of
distinguished objects can be chosen so that the square

```
⊕_l j_{W_l!} O_{W_l} ⟶ ⊕_i ⊕_{k ∈ K'_i} j_{U_ik!} O_{U_ik}
      |                             |
      v                             v
⊕_j j_{V_j!} O_{V_j} ------ f ----> ⊕_i j_{U_i!} O_{U_i}
```

commutes and induces an isomorphism on the cokernels of its horizontal maps. In other words
the presentation of `Coker f` may be refined along the given coverings of its generators.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.refinementAugmentation`: the right-hand vertical map
  `⊕_i ⊕_k j_{U_ik!} O_{U_ik} ⟶ ⊕_i j_{U_i!} O_{U_i}` of the square.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.blockInclusion`: the inclusion of the block of index `i` into its
  source.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.cechRelation`: the Čech relation attached to a pair of indices of the
  covering of `U_i`, read as a relation among the refined generators.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.refinedObjects`, `Stacks.SheafOfModules.refinedRelations` and
  `Stacks.SheafOfModules.refinedLifts`: the objects `W_l` and the two maps out of
  `⊕_l j_{W_l!} O_{W_l}` that the proof produces.

## Main results

* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.isIso_cokernelMap`: the abstract step. In any category with zero
  morphisms, a commutative square whose two vertical maps `p` and `q` are epimorphisms and for
  which the quotient map `cokernel.π g` factors through `q` induces an isomorphism on the
  cokernels of its horizontal maps.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.isIso_cokernelMap_refinementAugmentation`: the geometric step. If
  every Čech relation of every covering is killed by `cokernel.π g`, the factorisation the
  abstract step asks for exists.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.exists_refinement_isIso_cokernelMap`: the refinement exists when the
  coverings are already finite and their fibre products are quasi-compact.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.exists_finite_refinement_isIso_cokernelMap`: **Stacks Project,
  Tag 093F.**

## Implementation notes

**The abstract step is stated with the factorisation, not with the kernel.** Stacks omits the
details of this step; its content is that `ker q` is generated by the Čech relations. Written
that way the hypothesis reads `kernel.ι q ≫ cokernel.π g = 0` and the proof needs an abelian
category, since `q` epi then has to be presented as a cokernel of its own kernel
(`CategoryTheory.Abelian.epiDesc`). But in the application the section
`σ : ⊕_i j_{U_i!} O_{U_i} ⟶ Coker g` is produced *directly*, block by block, by the universal
property of the Čech sequence of Stacks 0934 — which is exactly a cokernel property — so taking
`σ` as the hypothesis both removes the abelian structure from the statement and removes a round
trip through `ker q` from the proof. In an abelian category the two forms are equivalent.

**Why the refined covering family is existentially re-bound.** Stacks 093F quantifies over
subfamilies `K'_i ⊆ K_i`. Spelling the subfamily as `(𝒰 i).restrictIndex Subtype.val` inside
every coproduct of the conclusion makes it unreadable, and — worse — puts two spellings of one
object into circulation, since `restrictIndex` composes the object map with the inclusion. The
conclusion therefore binds the refined family `𝒱` as data together with the equation
identifying it with the subfamily. That equation determines `𝒱` uniquely, so nothing is left
open, and every coproduct in the statement and in the proof is written in the one spelling
`(𝒱 i).X`.

**The index type of the refined family of objects is `Type (max u₁ v₁)`**, as in
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.exists_finite_lift_extensionByZeroUnit`: that is the universe in which
`CategoryTheory.GrothendieckTopology.IsQuasiCompactObject` and
`Stacks.QuasiCompactObjectsSituation.HasEnoughObjects` produce their index sets, so it is the
universe the applications of Stacks 0G1W land in. The family is finite, so this is a spelling
of the index set rather than a constraint on it.

**What the three conditions of Stacks 0937 are used for.** Condition (2) cuts each given
covering down to a finite subfamily which is still a covering, and supplies the
quasi-compactness of the `V_j` that the lifting step needs. Condition (3) supplies the fibre
products `U_ik ×_{U_i} U_ik'` themselves — a Grothendieck topology provides no pullbacks — and
their quasi-compactness, which is what lets the last application of Stacks 0G1W replace them by
distinguished objects. Condition (1) refines the coverings produced by local surjectivity and
by that last step so that their members are distinguished.

**Stacks' two lifting steps are one here.** The source says: find coverings `{V_jm → V_j}` on
which the generators of `⊕_j j_{V_j!} O_{V_j}` lift through the augmentation, then cut them down
to finite subfamilies `M'_j` by Stacks 0G1W. Both steps together are
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.exists_finite_lift_extensionByZeroUnit`, which already returns a finite
family of distinguished objects carrying the lifts.

The module universe is `max u₁ v₁ w t`, the universe at which
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.extensionByZeroUnit` is constructed and at which `Mod(R)` is abelian;
the two `local instance`s below are the same derivation that `ExtensionByZeroUnit.lean`,
`ExtensionByZeroQuasiCompact.lean`, `ExtensionByZeroUnitULift.lean`, `ExtensionByZeroCech.lean`
and `FiniteExtensionByZeroPresentation.lean` also carry privately; a public declaration of
another module cannot refer to a `private` one. If they are ever made public, all six copies
should cite them.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 093F](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/093F)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0937](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0937)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0934](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0934)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0G1V](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0G1V)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0G1W](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0G1W)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory Limits Opposite

universe u₁ v₁ w t

namespace Stacks.SheafOfModules

/-! ### The abstract step -/

section AbstractCokernel

variable {𝒜 : Type*} [Category 𝒜] [HasZeroMorphisms 𝒜]

/-- **The abstract step of Stacks 093F.** Let
```
W --g--> A'
|        |
p        q
v        v
B --f--> A
```
be a commutative square whose vertical maps `p` and `q` are epimorphisms, and suppose that the
quotient map `cokernel.π g` factors through `q`, say as `q ≫ σ`. Then the induced map
`Coker g ⟶ Coker f` is an isomorphism.

In an abelian category the hypothesis on `σ` is equivalent to `kernel.ι q ≫ cokernel.π g = 0`,
i.e. to `ker q` being generated by the relations in `W`; see the implementation notes. -/
theorem isIso_cokernelMap {W A' B A : 𝒜} (g : W ⟶ A') (f : B ⟶ A) (p : W ⟶ B) (q : A' ⟶ A)
    [HasCokernel g] [HasCokernel f] (h : g ≫ q = p ≫ f) [Epi p] [Epi q]
    (σ : A ⟶ cokernel g) (hσ : q ≫ σ = cokernel.π g) :
    IsIso (cokernel.map g f p q h) := by
  have hfσ : f ≫ σ = 0 := by
    refine (cancel_epi p).1 ?_
    rw [comp_zero, ← Category.assoc, ← h, Category.assoc, hσ, cokernel.condition]
  refine ⟨⟨cokernel.desc f σ hfσ, ?_, ?_⟩⟩
  · refine (cancel_epi (cokernel.π g)).1 ?_
    rw [Category.comp_id, ← Category.assoc, cokernel.π_desc, Category.assoc, cokernel.π_desc, hσ]
  · refine (cancel_epi (cokernel.π f)).1 ?_
    rw [Category.comp_id, ← Category.assoc, cokernel.π_desc]
    refine (cancel_epi q).1 ?_
    rw [← Category.assoc, hσ, cokernel.π_desc]

end AbstractCokernel

variable {C : Type u₁} [Category.{v₁} C]

attribute [local instance] siteHasSheafify siteWEqualsLocallyBijective

/-! ### The refinement square -/

section Refinement

variable {J : GrothendieckTopology C} (R : Sheaf J RingCat.{w}) {n m : ℕ} {U : Fin n → C}
  (V : Fin m → C) (𝒱 : ∀ i, PreZeroHypercover.{max u₁ v₁} (U i))

/-- **The augmentation of a family of coverings.** The map
`⊕_i ⊕_k j_{U_ik!} O_{U_ik} ⟶ ⊕_i j_{U_i!} O_{U_i}` whose `(i, k)`-th summand is the
functoriality map of `U_ik → U_i` followed by the `i`-th inclusion. -/
noncomputable def refinementAugmentation :
    (∐ fun x : Σ i, (𝒱 i).I₀ ↦ extensionByZeroUnit.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R ((𝒱 x.1).X x.2)) ⟶
      ∐ fun i ↦ extensionByZeroUnit.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R (U i) :=
  Sigma.desc fun x ↦ extensionByZeroUnitMap.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R ((𝒱 x.1).f x.2) ≫
    Sigma.ι (fun i ↦ extensionByZeroUnit.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R (U i)) x.1

/-- The `(i, k)`-th summand of `refinementAugmentation` is the functoriality map of
`U_ik → U_i` followed by the `i`-th inclusion. -/
@[reassoc]
lemma ι_comp_refinementAugmentation (x : Σ i, (𝒱 i).I₀) :
    Sigma.ι (fun y : Σ i, (𝒱 i).I₀ ↦
          extensionByZeroUnit.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R ((𝒱 y.1).X y.2)) x ≫
        refinementAugmentation.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R 𝒱 =
      extensionByZeroUnitMap.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R ((𝒱 x.1).f x.2) ≫
        Sigma.ι (fun i ↦ extensionByZeroUnit.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R (U i)) x.1 :=
  Sigma.ι_desc _ _

/-- The inclusion of the block of index `i` into `⊕_i ⊕_k j_{U_ik!} O_{U_ik}`. -/
noncomputable def blockInclusion (i : Fin n) :
    (∐ fun k : (𝒱 i).I₀ ↦ extensionByZeroUnit.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R ((𝒱 i).X k)) ⟶
      ∐ fun x : Σ i, (𝒱 i).I₀ ↦ extensionByZeroUnit.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R ((𝒱 x.1).X x.2) :=
  Sigma.desc fun k ↦ Sigma.ι (fun y : Σ i, (𝒱 i).I₀ ↦
    extensionByZeroUnit.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R ((𝒱 y.1).X y.2)) ⟨i, k⟩

/-- On the `k`-th summand, `blockInclusion` is the inclusion of the summand of index `(i, k)`. -/
@[reassoc]
lemma ι_comp_blockInclusion (i : Fin n) (k : (𝒱 i).I₀) :
    Sigma.ι (fun k' : (𝒱 i).I₀ ↦ extensionByZeroUnit.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R ((𝒱 i).X k')) k ≫
        blockInclusion.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R 𝒱 i =
      Sigma.ι (fun y : Σ i, (𝒱 i).I₀ ↦
        extensionByZeroUnit.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R ((𝒱 y.1).X y.2)) ⟨i, k⟩ :=
  Sigma.ι_desc _ _

/-- The restriction of `refinementAugmentation` to the block of index `i` is the augmentation
`⊕_k j_{U_ik!} O_{U_ik} ⟶ j_{U_i!} O_{U_i}` of the covering `𝒱 i` followed by the `i`-th
inclusion. -/
lemma blockInclusion_comp_refinementAugmentation (i : Fin n) :
    blockInclusion.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R 𝒱 i ≫ refinementAugmentation.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R 𝒱 =
      (Sigma.desc fun k ↦ extensionByZeroUnitMap.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R ((𝒱 i).f k)) ≫
        Sigma.ι (fun i' ↦ extensionByZeroUnit.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R (U i')) i := by
  refine Sigma.hom_ext _ _ fun k ↦ ?_
  rw [ι_comp_blockInclusion_assoc, ι_comp_refinementAugmentation, Sigma.ι_desc_assoc]

variable [∀ i, (𝒱 i).HasPullbacks]

/-- **A Čech relation among the refined generators.** The relation attached to a pair `(k, k')`
of indices of the covering of `U_i`: the difference of the two maps
`j_{U_ik ×_{U_i} U_ik'!} O ⟶ ⊕_i ⊕_k j_{U_ik!} O_{U_ik}` through the `(i, k)`-th and the
`(i, k')`-th summand. -/
noncomputable def cechRelation (i : Fin n) (pp : (𝒱 i).I₀ × (𝒱 i).I₀) :
    extensionByZeroUnit.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R (pullback ((𝒱 i).f pp.1) ((𝒱 i).f pp.2)) ⟶
      ∐ fun x : Σ i, (𝒱 i).I₀ ↦ extensionByZeroUnit.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R ((𝒱 x.1).X x.2) :=
  Sigma.ι (fun pq : (𝒱 i).I₀ × (𝒱 i).I₀ ↦ extensionByZeroUnit.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R
      (pullback ((𝒱 i).f pq.1) ((𝒱 i).f pq.2))) pp ≫
    cechRelationsMap.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R (𝒱 i) ≫ blockInclusion.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R 𝒱 i

/-- The Čech relations are relations: they are killed by the augmentation. -/
@[reassoc]
lemma cechRelation_comp_refinementAugmentation (i : Fin n) (pp : (𝒱 i).I₀ × (𝒱 i).I₀) :
    cechRelation.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R 𝒱 i pp ≫ refinementAugmentation.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R 𝒱 = 0 := by
  rw [cechRelation, Category.assoc, Category.assoc, blockInclusion_comp_refinementAugmentation,
    ← Category.assoc (cechRelationsMap.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R (𝒱 i)),
    cechRelationsMap_comp_sigmaDesc, zero_comp, comp_zero]

/-- A morphism out of `⊕_i ⊕_k j_{U_ik!} O_{U_ik}` which kills every Čech relation of the
`i`-th covering kills the whole Čech relations map of that covering. -/
lemma cechRelationsMap_comp_blockInclusion_comp (i : Fin n)
    {N : SheafOfModules.{max u₁ v₁ w t} R}
    (φ : (∐ fun x : Σ i, (𝒱 i).I₀ ↦
      extensionByZeroUnit.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R ((𝒱 x.1).X x.2)) ⟶ N)
    (hφ : ∀ pp, cechRelation.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R 𝒱 i pp ≫ φ = 0) :
    cechRelationsMap.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R (𝒱 i) ≫
      blockInclusion.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R 𝒱 i ≫ φ = 0 := by
  refine Sigma.hom_ext _ _ fun pp ↦ ?_
  rw [comp_zero, ← Category.assoc, ← Category.assoc]
  exact hφ pp

/-- A Čech relation dies in `Coker g` as soon as it does so after restriction along an
epimorphism which lifts through `g`. This is how the last application of Stacks 0G1W enters:
the fibre products `U_ik ×_{U_i} U_ik'` need not be distinguished, but they are quasi-compact,
so finitely many distinguished objects already map onto their extensions by zero. -/
lemma cechRelation_comp_cokernelπ_eq_zero (i : Fin n) (pp : (𝒱 i).I₀ × (𝒱 i).I₀)
    {D E : SheafOfModules.{max u₁ v₁ w t} R}
    (g : D ⟶ ∐ fun x : Σ i, (𝒱 i).I₀ ↦
      extensionByZeroUnit.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R ((𝒱 x.1).X x.2))
    (ε : E ⟶ extensionByZeroUnit.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R
      (pullback ((𝒱 i).f pp.1) ((𝒱 i).f pp.2))) [Epi ε] (ν : E ⟶ D)
    (hν : ν ≫ g = ε ≫ cechRelation.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R 𝒱 i pp) :
    cechRelation.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R 𝒱 i pp ≫ cokernel.π g = 0 := by
  refine (cancel_epi ε).1 ?_
  rw [comp_zero, ← Category.assoc, ← hν, Category.assoc, cokernel.condition, comp_zero]

/-- **The geometric step of Stacks 093F.** Suppose that every Čech relation of every covering
`𝒱 i` is killed by `cokernel.π g`, i.e. that the relations of the refined presentation already
contain the relations among the refined generators. Then the square induces an isomorphism on
the cokernels of its horizontal maps.

The section required by `Stacks.SheafOfModules.isIso_cokernelMap` is produced block by block by
the universal property of the Čech sequence of Stacks 0934. -/
theorem isIso_cokernelMap_refinementAugmentation
    (h𝒱cov : ∀ i, (𝒱 i).sieve₀ ∈ J (U i))
    {D B : SheafOfModules.{max u₁ v₁ w t} R}
    (g : D ⟶ ∐ fun x : Σ i, (𝒱 i).I₀ ↦
      extensionByZeroUnit.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R ((𝒱 x.1).X x.2))
    (f : B ⟶ ∐ fun i ↦ extensionByZeroUnit.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R (U i)) (p : D ⟶ B)
    (h : g ≫ refinementAugmentation.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R 𝒱 = p ≫ f) [Epi p]
    [Epi (refinementAugmentation.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R 𝒱)]
    (hrel : ∀ i pp, cechRelation.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R 𝒱 i pp ≫ cokernel.π g = 0) :
    IsIso (cokernel.map g f p (refinementAugmentation.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R 𝒱) h) := by
  choose σ hσ using fun i ↦ exists_hom_of_cechRelationsMap_comp_eq_zero.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R (𝒱 i)
    (h𝒱cov i) (blockInclusion.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R 𝒱 i ≫ cokernel.π g)
    (cechRelationsMap_comp_blockInclusion_comp.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R 𝒱 i _ (hrel i))
  refine isIso_cokernelMap _ _ _ _ h (Sigma.desc σ) (Sigma.hom_ext _ _ fun x ↦ ?_)
  rw [ι_comp_refinementAugmentation_assoc, Sigma.ι_desc]
  have hx := Sigma.ι (fun k ↦ extensionByZeroUnit.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R ((𝒱 x.1).X k)) x.2 ≫= hσ x.1
  rw [Sigma.ι_desc_assoc, ι_comp_blockInclusion_assoc] at hx
  exact hx

/-! ### The refined square -/

variable (κ : ∀ i, (𝒱 i).I₀ × (𝒱 i).I₀ → Type (max u₁ v₁)) (Y : ∀ i pp, κ i pp → C)
  (M : Fin m → Type (max u₁ v₁)) (Z : ∀ j, M j → C)

/-- **The objects of the refined family of Stacks 093F.** The objects `Y i (k, k') c` covering
the fibre product `U_ik ×_{U_i} U_ik'`, together with the objects `Z j c` covering `V j` over
which the `j`-th generator of the source lifts.

This is an `abbrev`, and it is written with `Sum.rec` rather than `Sum.elim`, so that
`refinedObjects … (Sum.inl x)` reduces to `Y x.1 x.2.1 x.2.2` at `reducible` transparency. A
semireducible definition here would leave every morphism out of a single summand with two
definitionally-equal but syntactically-different source objects, after which `rw` refuses to
fire on the goal with "the target expression is not type-correct under the `implicit`
transparency level". -/
abbrev refinedObjects :
    ((i : Fin n) × (pp : (𝒱 i).I₀ × (𝒱 i).I₀) × κ i pp) ⊕ ((j : Fin m) × M j) → C :=
  Sum.rec (fun x ↦ Y x.1 x.2.1 x.2.2) fun x ↦ Z x.1 x.2

/-- **The horizontal map of the refined square.** Its summands are the refined Čech relations
of the coverings `𝒱 i` and the chosen lifts `d j c` of the generators of the source. -/
noncomputable def refinedRelations
    (y : ∀ i pp c, Y i pp c ⟶ pullback ((𝒱 i).f pp.1) ((𝒱 i).f pp.2))
    (d : ∀ j c, extensionByZeroUnit.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R (Z j c) ⟶
      ∐ fun x : Σ i, (𝒱 i).I₀ ↦ extensionByZeroUnit.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R ((𝒱 x.1).X x.2)) :
    (∐ fun l ↦ extensionByZeroUnit.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R (refinedObjects 𝒱 κ Y M Z l)) ⟶
      ∐ fun x : Σ i, (𝒱 i).I₀ ↦ extensionByZeroUnit.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R ((𝒱 x.1).X x.2) :=
  Sigma.desc (Sum.rec (fun x ↦ extensionByZeroUnitMap.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R (y x.1 x.2.1 x.2.2) ≫
    cechRelation.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R 𝒱 x.1 x.2.1) fun x ↦ d x.1 x.2)

variable (y : ∀ i pp c, Y i pp c ⟶ pullback ((𝒱 i).f pp.1) ((𝒱 i).f pp.2))
  (d : ∀ j c, extensionByZeroUnit.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R (Z j c) ⟶
    ∐ fun x : Σ i, (𝒱 i).I₀ ↦ extensionByZeroUnit.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R ((𝒱 x.1).X x.2))

/-- On the summand of a refined Čech relation, `refinedRelations` is the functoriality map of
`y` followed by the corresponding Čech relation. -/
@[reassoc]
lemma ι_inl_comp_refinedRelations (x : (i : Fin n) × (pp : (𝒱 i).I₀ × (𝒱 i).I₀) × κ i pp) :
    Sigma.ι (fun l ↦ extensionByZeroUnit.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R
          (refinedObjects 𝒱 κ Y M Z l)) (Sum.inl x) ≫
        refinedRelations.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R 𝒱 κ Y M Z y d =
      extensionByZeroUnitMap.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R (y x.1 x.2.1 x.2.2) ≫
        cechRelation.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R 𝒱 x.1 x.2.1 :=
  Sigma.ι_desc _ _

/-- On the summand of index `(j, c)`, `refinedRelations` is the chosen lift `d j c`. -/
@[reassoc]
lemma ι_inr_comp_refinedRelations (x : (j : Fin m) × M j) :
    Sigma.ι (fun l ↦ extensionByZeroUnit.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R
          (refinedObjects 𝒱 κ Y M Z l)) (Sum.inr x) ≫
        refinedRelations.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R 𝒱 κ Y M Z y d = d x.1 x.2 :=
  Sigma.ι_desc _ _

/-- **The left-hand vertical map of the refined square.** It is zero on the summands carrying
the Čech relations and the functoriality map of `Z j c → V j` on the others. -/
noncomputable def refinedLifts (g' : ∀ j c, Z j c ⟶ V j) :
    (∐ fun l ↦ extensionByZeroUnit.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R (refinedObjects 𝒱 κ Y M Z l)) ⟶
      ∐ fun j ↦ extensionByZeroUnit.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R (V j) :=
  Sigma.desc (Sum.rec (fun _ ↦ 0) fun x ↦ extensionByZeroUnitMap.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R (g' x.1 x.2) ≫
    Sigma.ι (fun j ↦ extensionByZeroUnit.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R (V j)) x.1)

variable (g' : ∀ j c, Z j c ⟶ V j)

omit [∀ i, (𝒱 i).HasPullbacks] in
/-- `refinedLifts` vanishes on the summands carrying the refined Čech relations. -/
lemma ι_inl_comp_refinedLifts (x : (i : Fin n) × (pp : (𝒱 i).I₀ × (𝒱 i).I₀) × κ i pp) :
    Sigma.ι (fun l ↦ extensionByZeroUnit.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R
          (refinedObjects 𝒱 κ Y M Z l)) (Sum.inl x) ≫
        refinedLifts.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R V 𝒱 κ Y M Z g' = 0 :=
  Sigma.ι_desc _ _

omit [∀ i, (𝒱 i).HasPullbacks] in
/-- On the summand of index `(j, c)`, `refinedLifts` is the functoriality map of `Z j c → V j`
followed by the `j`-th inclusion. -/
@[reassoc]
lemma ι_inr_comp_refinedLifts (x : (j : Fin m) × M j) :
    Sigma.ι (fun l ↦ extensionByZeroUnit.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R
          (refinedObjects 𝒱 κ Y M Z l)) (Sum.inr x) ≫
        refinedLifts.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R V 𝒱 κ Y M Z g' =
      extensionByZeroUnitMap.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R (g' x.1 x.2) ≫
        Sigma.ι (fun j ↦ extensionByZeroUnit.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R (V j)) x.1 :=
  Sigma.ι_desc _ _

/-- The refined square commutes: the Čech relations are killed by the augmentation, and the
chosen lifts commute with it by construction. -/
lemma refinedRelations_comp_refinementAugmentation
    (f : (∐ fun j ↦ extensionByZeroUnit.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R (V j)) ⟶
      ∐ fun i ↦ extensionByZeroUnit.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R (U i))
    (hd : ∀ j c, d j c ≫ refinementAugmentation.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R 𝒱 =
      extensionByZeroUnitMap.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R (g' j c) ≫
        Sigma.ι (fun j' ↦ extensionByZeroUnit.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R (V j')) j ≫ f) :
    refinedRelations.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R 𝒱 κ Y M Z y d ≫
        refinementAugmentation.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R 𝒱 =
      refinedLifts.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R V 𝒱 κ Y M Z g' ≫ f := by
  refine Sigma.hom_ext _ _ fun l ↦ ?_
  cases l with
  | inl x =>
      rw [ι_inl_comp_refinedRelations_assoc, ← Category.assoc
        (Sigma.ι (fun l ↦ extensionByZeroUnit.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R
          (refinedObjects 𝒱 κ Y M Z l)) (Sum.inl x)),
        ι_inl_comp_refinedLifts, zero_comp, cechRelation_comp_refinementAugmentation, comp_zero]
  | inr x =>
      rw [ι_inr_comp_refinedRelations_assoc, ι_inr_comp_refinedLifts_assoc]
      exact hd x.1 x.2

omit [∀ i, (𝒱 i).HasPullbacks] in
/-- The left-hand vertical map of the refined square is an epimorphism: it is so already on the
summands carrying the lifted generators. -/
lemma epi_refinedLifts
    (hepi : Epi (Sigma.desc fun x : (j : Fin m) × M j ↦
      extensionByZeroUnitMap.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R (g' x.1 x.2) ≫
        Sigma.ι (fun j ↦ extensionByZeroUnit.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R (V j)) x.1)) :
    Epi (refinedLifts.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R V 𝒱 κ Y M Z g') := by
  have he : (Sigma.desc fun x : (j : Fin m) × M j ↦
        Sigma.ι (fun l ↦ extensionByZeroUnit.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R
          (refinedObjects 𝒱 κ Y M Z l)) (Sum.inr x)) ≫
        refinedLifts.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R V 𝒱 κ Y M Z g' =
      Sigma.desc fun x : (j : Fin m) × M j ↦
        extensionByZeroUnitMap.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R (g' x.1 x.2) ≫
          Sigma.ι (fun j ↦ extensionByZeroUnit.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R (V j)) x.1 :=
    Sigma.hom_ext _ _ fun x ↦ by
      rw [Sigma.ι_desc_assoc, ι_inr_comp_refinedLifts, Sigma.ι_desc]
  have hcomp : Epi ((Sigma.desc fun x : (j : Fin m) × M j ↦
      Sigma.ι (fun l ↦ extensionByZeroUnit.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R
        (refinedObjects 𝒱 κ Y M Z l)) (Sum.inr x)) ≫
      refinedLifts.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R V 𝒱 κ Y M Z g') := by
    rw [he]; exact hepi
  exact epi_of_epi (Sigma.desc fun x : (j : Fin m) × M j ↦
    Sigma.ι (fun l ↦ extensionByZeroUnit.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R
      (refinedObjects 𝒱 κ Y M Z l)) (Sum.inr x)) _

end Refinement

/-! ### Stacks 093F -/

section Existence

variable (S : QuasiCompactObjectsSituation C) (R : Sheaf S.topology RingCat.{w})

/-- **Stacks 093F for coverings which are already finite.** Given a morphism
`f : ⊕_j j_{V_j!} O_{V_j} ⟶ ⊕_i j_{U_i!} O_{U_i}` with the `V_j` distinguished, and finite
coverings `𝒱 i` of the `U_i` whose pairwise fibre products exist and are quasi-compact, there is
a finite family `{W_l}` of distinguished objects and a commutative square over `f` whose
right-hand vertical map is the augmentation of the `𝒱 i`, and which induces an isomorphism on
the cokernels of its horizontal maps.

The `W_l` are of two kinds: distinguished objects covering the fibre products
`U_ik ×_{U_i} U_ik'`, and distinguished objects covering the `V_j` over which the generators of
the source lift through the augmentation. -/
theorem exists_refinement_isIso_cokernelMap
    (hEnough : S.HasEnoughObjects) (hqc : S.ObjectsAreQuasiCompact)
    {n m : ℕ} {U : Fin n → C} (V : Fin m → C) (hV : ∀ j, V j ∈ S.objects)
    (𝒱 : ∀ i, PreZeroHypercover.{max u₁ v₁} (U i))
    [∀ i, Finite (𝒱 i).I₀] [∀ i, (𝒱 i).HasPullbacks]
    (h𝒱cov : ∀ i, (𝒱 i).sieve₀ ∈ S.topology (U i))
    (hpbqc : ∀ i (k k' : (𝒱 i).I₀),
      S.topology.IsQuasiCompactObject (pullback ((𝒱 i).f k) ((𝒱 i).f k')))
    (f : (∐ fun j ↦ extensionByZeroUnit.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R (V j)) ⟶
      ∐ fun i ↦ extensionByZeroUnit.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R (U i)) :
    ∃ (L : Type (max u₁ v₁)) (_ : Finite L) (W : L → C), (∀ l, W l ∈ S.objects) ∧
      ∃ (g : (∐ fun l ↦ extensionByZeroUnit.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R (W l)) ⟶
            ∐ fun x : Σ i, (𝒱 i).I₀ ↦ extensionByZeroUnit.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R ((𝒱 x.1).X x.2))
          (p : (∐ fun l ↦ extensionByZeroUnit.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R (W l)) ⟶
            ∐ fun j ↦ extensionByZeroUnit.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R (V j)),
        g ≫ refinementAugmentation.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R 𝒱 = p ≫ f ∧
          Epi (refinementAugmentation.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R 𝒱) ∧
          ∀ h : g ≫ refinementAugmentation.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R 𝒱 = p ≫ f,
            IsIso (cokernel.map g f p (refinementAugmentation.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R 𝒱) h) := by
  classical
  have hq : Epi (refinementAugmentation.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R 𝒱) :=
    epi_sigmaDesc_sigmaIota S R U (fun i ↦ (𝒱 i).I₀) (fun i k ↦ (𝒱 i).X k)
      (fun i k ↦ (𝒱 i).f k)
      fun i ↦ epi_sigmaDesc_extensionByZeroUnitMap.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R (𝒱 i) (h𝒱cov i)
  choose M hM Zv gv hZv hgvepi d hd using fun j ↦
    exists_finite_lift_extensionByZeroUnit.{u₁, v₁, w, t} S R hEnough hqc
      (refinementAugmentation.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R 𝒱) (hV j)
      (Sigma.ι (fun j' ↦ extensionByZeroUnit.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R (V j')) j ≫ f)
  choose 𝒲 h𝒲cov h𝒲obj using fun (i : Fin n) (pp : (𝒱 i).I₀ × (𝒱 i).I₀) ↦
    hEnough (pullback ((𝒱 i).f pp.1) ((𝒱 i).f pp.2))
  choose N hNfin hNepi using fun (i : Fin n) (pp : (𝒱 i).I₀ × (𝒱 i).I₀) ↦
    exists_finite_epi_sigmaDesc_extensionByZeroUnitMap.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R
      (hpbqc i pp.1 pp.2) (𝒲 i pp) (h𝒲cov i pp)
  have _ : ∀ j, Finite (M j) := hM
  have _ : ∀ i pp, Finite ↥(N i pp) := fun i pp ↦ (hNfin i pp).to_subtype
  have hLfin : Finite ((((i : Fin n) × (pp : (𝒱 i).I₀ × (𝒱 i).I₀) × ↥(N i pp))) ⊕
      ((j : Fin m) × M j)) := inferInstance
  have hobj : ∀ l, refinedObjects 𝒱 (fun i pp ↦ ↥(N i pp))
      (fun i pp c ↦ (𝒲 i pp).X c.1) M Zv l ∈ S.objects := by
    rintro (x | x)
    exacts [h𝒲obj _ _ _, hZv _ _]
  have hcm := refinedRelations_comp_refinementAugmentation.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R V 𝒱
    (fun i pp ↦ ↥(N i pp)) (fun i pp c ↦ (𝒲 i pp).X c.1) M Zv
    (fun i pp c ↦ (𝒲 i pp).f c.1) d gv f hd
  refine ⟨_, hLfin, _, hobj, _, _, hcm, hq, fun h ↦ ?_⟩
  have _ := hq
  have _ : Epi (refinedLifts.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R V 𝒱 (fun i pp ↦ ↥(N i pp))
      (fun i pp c ↦ (𝒲 i pp).X c.1) M Zv gv) :=
    epi_refinedLifts.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R V 𝒱 (fun i pp ↦ ↥(N i pp))
      (fun i pp c ↦ (𝒲 i pp).X c.1) M Zv gv
      (epi_sigmaDesc_sigmaIota S R V M Zv gv hgvepi)
  refine isIso_cokernelMap_refinementAugmentation.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R 𝒱 h𝒱cov _ f _ h
    fun i pp ↦ ?_
  have _ := hNepi i pp
  refine cechRelation_comp_cokernelπ_eq_zero.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R 𝒱 i pp _
    (Sigma.desc fun c : ↥(N i pp) ↦
      extensionByZeroUnitMap.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R ((𝒲 i pp).f c.1))
    (Sigma.desc fun c : ↥(N i pp) ↦ Sigma.ι (fun l ↦ extensionByZeroUnit.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R
      (refinedObjects 𝒱 (fun i pp ↦ ↥(N i pp))
        (fun i pp c ↦ (𝒲 i pp).X c.1) M Zv l)) (Sum.inl ⟨i, pp, c⟩))
    (Sigma.hom_ext _ _ fun c ↦ ?_)
  rw [Sigma.ι_desc_assoc, Sigma.ι_desc_assoc]
  exact ι_inl_comp_refinedRelations.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R 𝒱 (fun i pp ↦ ↥(N i pp))
    (fun i pp c ↦ (𝒲 i pp).X c.1) M Zv (fun i pp c ↦ (𝒲 i pp).f c.1) d ⟨i, pp, c⟩

/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 093F.** A finite presentation by extensions by zero can be changed
along coverings of its target generators without changing its cokernel: finite subfamilies
`K'_i` of the given coverings and a finite family `{W_l}` of distinguished objects can be chosen
so that the resulting square over `f` induces an isomorphism on the cokernels of its horizontal
maps. -/
@[stacks 093F]
theorem exists_finite_refinement_isIso_cokernelMap
    (hEnough : S.HasEnoughObjects) (hqc : S.ObjectsAreQuasiCompact)
    (hqs : S.CoverPullbacksAreQuasiCompact)
    {n m : ℕ} {U : Fin n → C} (V : Fin m → C)
    (hU : ∀ i, U i ∈ S.objects) (hV : ∀ j, V j ∈ S.objects)
    (𝒰 : ∀ i, PreZeroHypercover.{max u₁ v₁} (U i))
    (h𝒰 : ∀ i, (𝒰 i).sieve₀ ∈ S.topology (U i))
    (h𝒰obj : ∀ i k, (𝒰 i).X k ∈ S.objects)
    (f : (∐ fun j ↦ extensionByZeroUnit.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R (V j)) ⟶
      ∐ fun i ↦ extensionByZeroUnit.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R (U i)) :
    ∃ (T : ∀ i, Set (𝒰 i).I₀) (𝒱 : ∀ i, PreZeroHypercover.{max u₁ v₁} (U i)),
      (∀ i, (T i).Finite) ∧
        (∀ i, 𝒱 i = (𝒰 i).restrictIndex (Subtype.val : T i → (𝒰 i).I₀)) ∧
        (∀ i, (𝒱 i).sieve₀ ∈ S.topology (U i)) ∧
        ∃ (L : Type (max u₁ v₁)) (_ : Finite L) (W : L → C), (∀ l, W l ∈ S.objects) ∧
          ∃ (g : (∐ fun l ↦ extensionByZeroUnit.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R (W l)) ⟶
                ∐ fun x : Σ i, (𝒱 i).I₀ ↦ extensionByZeroUnit.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R ((𝒱 x.1).X x.2))
              (p : (∐ fun l ↦ extensionByZeroUnit.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R (W l)) ⟶
                ∐ fun j ↦ extensionByZeroUnit.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R (V j)),
            g ≫ refinementAugmentation.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R 𝒱 = p ≫ f ∧
              Epi (refinementAugmentation.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R 𝒱) ∧
              ∀ h : g ≫ refinementAugmentation.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R 𝒱 = p ≫ f,
                IsIso (cokernel.map g f p (refinementAugmentation.{u₁, v₁, w, t} R 𝒱) h) := by
  classical
  choose T hTfin hTcov using fun i ↦ QuasiCompact.exists_finite_restrictIndex_sieve₀_mem
    (hqc (U i) (hU i)) (𝒰 i) (h𝒰 i)
  have _ : ∀ i, Finite ((𝒰 i).restrictIndex (Subtype.val : T i → (𝒰 i).I₀)).I₀ :=
    fun i ↦ (hTfin i).to_subtype
  have hpb : ∀ i, ((𝒰 i).restrictIndex (Subtype.val : T i → (𝒰 i).I₀)).HasPullbacks :=
    fun i k k' ↦ (hqs (U i) _ (hTcov i) (hU i) (fun c ↦ h𝒰obj i c.1) k k').1
  have hpbqc : ∀ i (k k' : ((𝒰 i).restrictIndex (Subtype.val : T i → (𝒰 i).I₀)).I₀),
      S.topology.IsQuasiCompactObject (pullback
        (((𝒰 i).restrictIndex (Subtype.val : T i → (𝒰 i).I₀)).f k)
        (((𝒰 i).restrictIndex (Subtype.val : T i → (𝒰 i).I₀)).f k')) := by
    intro i k k'
    have _ := hpb i
    exact (hqs (U i) _ (hTcov i) (hU i) (fun c ↦ h𝒰obj i c.1) k k').2
  obtain ⟨L, hL, W, hW, g, p, hcomm, hepi, hiso⟩ :=
    exists_refinement_isIso_cokernelMap.{u₁, v₁, w, t} S R hEnough hqc V hV
      (fun i ↦ (𝒰 i).restrictIndex (Subtype.val : T i → (𝒰 i).I₀)) hTcov hpbqc f
  exact ⟨T, fun i ↦ (𝒰 i).restrictIndex (Subtype.val : T i → (𝒰 i).I₀), hTfin, fun i ↦ rfl,
    hTcov, L, hL, W, hW, g, p, hcomm, hepi, hiso⟩

end Existence

end Stacks.SheafOfModules

